Phase 3.1 Known Issues and Limitations
======================================

CURRENT LIMITATIONS
-------------------
1. Multiprocess race conditions not fully exhaustive
   - Current tests use fork-based multiprocessing
   - True distributed race testing would need separate machines
   - Lease break_stale edge cases under extreme clock skew not tested
   - Scheduler bounded concurrency only tested with fork, not true distributed

2. Lease expiry and clock dependency
   - Lease TTL based on time.time() - clock skew between processes could cause
     premature expiry or extended holds
   - break_stale requires now >= expires_at - system clock accuracy matters
   - No testing with NTP-disynchronized clocks

3. True distributed scheduler not implemented
   - Scheduler is local-bounded-concurrency only
   - No multi-node task coordination
   - No network-based lease arbitration
   - Phase 4 would address distributed coordination

4. Import conservatism could block legitimate use cases
   - Refusing task-id conflicts means identical goals can't be re-imported
   - No merge or conflict resolution strategy
   - Designed for safety over flexibility

5. Dead-letter state manual activation required
   - dead_letter() requires can_transition check
   - No automatic dead-lettering on repeated failures
   - Manual operator decision via requires_user_decision

6. Dependency checking linear only
   - depends_on checks all dependencies COMPLETED
   - No circular dependency detection
   - No transitive dependency optimization

7. Lineage traversal is O(n) in number of tasks
   - Not optimized for large task trees
   - All tasks scanned for parent_task_id matches
   - Phase 4 would add indexing

8. No encryption at rest for stored data
   - Task JSONL, audit JSONL, receipts JSONL all plain text
   - SQLite stored without encryption
   - For production use, external encryption layer needed

9. No backup encryption or compression
   - backup_directory writes raw JSONL
   - No gzip/zlib compression
   - No AES or other encryption in backup pipeline
   - Tamper detection available but not encrypted

10. Retry/recovery opt-in not clearly documented
    - retry_safe default False per capability
    - Users must check capability specs for retry_safe/replay_safe
    - Discovery mechanism not built into CLI

